{
  "id": "sensory-substitution",
  "term": "sensory substitution",
  "definition": "Sensory substitution is the use of a device or method that delivers information usually received through one sense, especially vision, through another sense such as hearing or touch. In this context, it refers to systems that translate visual input into auditory or tactile signals so users can learn to identify visual information through a different sensory channel.",
